    {
      "id": "claim_8f12a2bb6b2f4e4f8ee86fa4ec4c70f3",
      "statement": "The llm package defines a provider-agnostic streaming chat interface: Driver has a single Stream(ctx, req) (PartStream, error) method; PartStream.Next blocks for the next Part and errors only when the context is done (ctx.Err) or after the final part (io.EOF); the final part carries Usage and Finish (stop|tool_calls|length|error), and Err is non-nil only on the final part after a 200 began.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/llm/llm.go#L63-L97",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:e1a4b21c61da1bd5a4bba8d69882eee8ac675aedfd0a55c1c736a118e8e72cd5:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_c7405e75465143faab247b01c6c48886",
      "statement": "The error model: APIError is a decoded non-2xx upstream response (Body capped at 64 KiB, Message the provider-decoded text, keeping the 'upstream error (http %d): ...' framing); TransientError wraps a retryable failure with its HTTP status; IsTransient reports a 429/5xx TransientError or a network error, and context errors are not transient — this is the predicate the engine's pre-stream retry uses.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://internal/llm/llm.go#L105-L144",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:3e68e910c40fe4656c601a5746624d43990ab419c919ae1204e93de25e28d914:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_65b61135718e48a4a0e2897185874b49",
      "statement": "upstreamError (shared by both drivers) drains the non-2xx body before close (capped at 64 KiB), decodes the provider message (the {\"error\":{...}} envelope first, then a plain-string error, then the trimmed body, then the status line), and returns *APIError — with 429/5xx wrapped in *TransientError.",
